## Transformation quick reference

Use SDK methods — not URL strings. Raw URL syntax (`c_fill`, `e_blur`, etc.) only belongs inside `addTransformation()`.

```tsx
// Resize to exact dimensions (smart crop)
cld.image('id').resize(fill().width(800).height(600))

// Resize by one dimension (preserves aspect ratio)
cld.image('id').resize(scale().width(400))

// Apply an effect
cld.image('id').effect(blur(800))

// Always end with format + quality (separate .delivery() calls)
.delivery(format(auto())).delivery(quality(autoQuality()))

// Raw URL escape hatch — for params the SDK doesn't expose directly
cld.image('id').addTransformation('e_background_removal')
```

**Import path gotcha** — wrong subpaths are the #1 source of "module not found" errors. Use the **Key import paths** table above exactly:
- `text`, `image` → `@cloudinary/url-gen/qualifiers/source` (**not** `actions/overlay`)
- `Position` → `@cloudinary/url-gen/qualifiers/position` (**not** `positioning/Position`)
- `AdvancedImage`, `AdvancedVideo`, plugins → `@cloudinary/react` (**not** `@cloudinary/url-gen`)

For overlays, use the canonical block in the `cloudinary-react` skill — do not derive paths.
